GoodHours / Hourly

A school service-hours platform for students, schools, and community partners.

Current status
- Active rework branch
- Customer-facing flow work is focused on signup/login, browse, signup/waitlist, and attendance verification
- Latest QA notes live in tests/qa-results.md

Local development (self-contained subshells; run in separate terminals)
- (cd client && npm run dev)
- (cd server && npm run dev)

Fresh clone setup (verified 2026-09-10 on Node v24.21.0, loopback disposable Postgres)

Prerequisites
- Node 24 (`node --version` must report v24.x; see `.nvmrc`) and npm 10+.
- A container runtime (`podman` or `docker`) for the disposable test/dev database.
  The server test suite starts it automatically (see `server/scripts/ensure-test-db.sh`).

Install (root first for shared tooling; every line is a self-contained subshell,
safe to paste sequentially)
- npm ci
- (cd server && npm ci)
- (cd client && npm ci)

Configure
- No manual secrets are needed for local testing: the tracked `server/.env.test`
  points at the disposable loopback database (`127.0.0.1:5433/goodhours_test`) and
  carries dummy-only credentials. Real environment variables always take precedence
  over that file when set, and CI sets its own `DATABASE_URL` instead.
- For local development against your own database, copy `server/.env.example` to
  `server/.env` and fill in real values there (never commit that file).

Verify (each line is a self-contained subshell, safe to paste sequentially)
- node --version   # must report v24.x (see .nvmrc)
- (cd server && node --env-file=.env.test node_modules/prisma/build/index.js validate --schema=prisma/schema.prisma)
  # loads the tracked dummy-only env file; no manual secrets needed
- (unset DATABASE_URL; cd server && npm test)
  # drops any inherited DATABASE_URL so the tracked loopback dummy applies.
  # `pretest` runs two harness scripts BEFORE any test process boots: it starts the
  # disposable DB if needed (`scripts/ensure-test-db.sh`), then fail-closed validates
  # every inherited database target and mode flag (`scripts/ensure-safe-test-target.sh`
  # refuses non-loopback DATABASE_URL/DEV_DATABASE_URL/RATE_LIMIT_TEST_DATABASE_URL
  # and any production APP_ENV/NODE_ENV/VERCEL_ENV). This pretest gate — not the pilot
  # test's own guard (which covers only its file, since node --test runs files
  # concurrently) — is what protects every concurrently running test. Server env
  # validation additionally refuses remote shared databases in development
  # (`server/src/lib/env.ts`).
  # To replay the refusal proof with a deliberately non-loopback dummy target
  # (`.invalid` never resolves, so refusal precedes any connection):
  # (cd server && DATABASE_URL='postgresql://user:pass@db.non-loopback.invalid:5432/prod' node --env-file-if-exists=.env.test --import tsx --test tests/syntheticSchoolPilot.integration.test.ts)
  # expected: non-zero exit with "pilot must use loopback DB".
- (cd server && npm run build)
- (cd client && npm run build)

Safety: these commands touch only the loopback/disposable database. Never point
`DATABASE_URL` at a shared or production database for local testing.

Production build
- (cd client && npm run build)
- (cd server && npm run build)

Notes
- Students browse school-approved opportunities and sign up or waitlist directly from the slot detail page.
- Students can check in, check out, and submit verification from the dashboard.
- School admins handle school registration and verification workflows.
